        ":question/id": "3bcbd307-7eb0-5749-9f39-f59ad0eeb13c",
        ":question/problem": "Find an antiderivative.\n\n$$\n\\int \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{16 - x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\n$$\n\nYou may use $\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u=\\arcsin{\\left(u \\right)}+C$.\n\nChoose the antiderivative. In each choice, $C$ is an arbitrary constant.",
        ":question/worked-solution": "Let $u=\\frac{x}{4}$. Then $\\mathrm{d}u=(\\frac{1}{4})\\,\\mathrm{d}x$.\n\nFactor the constant in the denominator:\n\n$$\n\\sqrt{16 - x^{2}}=4\\sqrt{1-(\\frac{x}{4})^2}.\n$$\n\nThe differential is $\\mathrm{d}x=4\\,\\mathrm{d}u$. The outside factor is $1\\cdot 4=4$.\n\nIncluding the differential factor gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}&\\int \\frac{4}{\\sqrt{16 - x^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x\\\\&=4\\left(\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right).\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nUse the supplied primitive:\n\n$$\n4\\left(\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{1 - u^{2}}}\\,\\mathrm{d}u\\right)=4\\left(\\arcsin{\\left(u \\right)}\\right)+C.\n$$\n\nSubstitute back:\n\n$$\n4\\left(\\arcsin{\\left(\\frac{x}{4} \\right)}\\right)+C.\n$$",
